    <p>The last roof you nailed down has always been your best salesman, and one that's held tight through five hail seasons sells harder than any ad. But the replacements coming due around Cullman aren't all names on your list. The family that bought an older place out toward Baileyton and just found granules pooling in the gutters doesn't know a roofer — they search. The couple who closed on a Smith Lake home and caught a hard hailstorm their first spring here has no neighbor to ask, so they turn to Google, where a chaser crew is already paying to appear. Those owners are the next wave of work, and not one of them runs through your referral chain, which is precisely <a href="/articles/why-word-of-mouth-isnt-enough/">the ceiling word of mouth hits</a> when the storms keep delivering customers who've never heard your name. The only thing waiting for them where they're looking is a real page.</p>

